  "id": "seated-machine-abdominal-crunch",
  "name": "Seated Machine Abdominal Crunch",
  "definition": "A seated spinal-flexion isolation on the exact Life Fitness Insignia SS-AB selectorized abdominal fixture. The athlete curls the upper torso while the hips remain seated and the arms guide the handles rather than drive the repetition. The manual and its start/finish diagrams establish the support and crunch topology; strict avoidance of deliberate hip-driven motion is a bounded technique choice, not a measured zero-pelvis-motion claim. Rectus abdominis is primary and obliques secondary by abdominal emphasis and existing spinal-flexion capabilities. Other abdominal machines, SS-ABD abdominal fixtures, cable crunches, floor curl-ups, and hip-driven sit-ups are excluded.",
  "evidenceRefs": [
    "life-fitness-2024-insignia-series-manual",
    "christophy-2012-lumbar-spine"
  ],
